{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkCiZw7DKUE8QtZUShw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Technically yes, since it's just a Durable Object stub and JS RPC works on any DO stub. In practice it's fragile. The Agents SDK (built on PartyServer) expects each Agent instance to have a **name**, which it normally gets through `getAgentByName()` / `idFromName()` or request routing (`routeAgentRequest`). An ID from `newUniqueId()` has no name. So any RPC method that touches name-dependent machinery, such as state, scheduling, or anything reading `this.name`, can throw an error like \"Attempting to read .name on … before it was set.\"\n\nThe recommended approach is to address Agents by name with `getAgentByName(env.MyAgent, someName)`. If you need uniqueness, generate a random string such as `crypto.randomUUID()` and use that as the name."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2259,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2259},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fecb4c72-0573-46a8-8634-4b2baa70e95e","uuid":"6c47199a-6920-4a3d-886f-213cd03674b1","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:10:00.370Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkCiKYCbb7y5ZFG5z5u"}
